   "hypothesis_id": "H3-Innate-Mucosal-IgA",
   "mechanism": "DEFA4 (an antimicrobial defensin), ITGAX (CD11c on dendritic cells), and CARD9 (a fungal pattern recognition mediator) are integral to the innate immune response against intestinal microbiota. Dysregulated sensing of the local microbiome by these genes alters mucosal immunity and triggers localized inflammation. This aberrant mucosal environment stimulates the anomalous production of undergalactosylated IgA1, linking intestinal immunity to systemic IgA glomerulonephritis.",
